    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"In Pakistan, less than 25 per cent of blood donations are voluntary and the supply of blood available in hospitals is far less than the demand from patients,\" said Dr Bushra Moiz, Consultant Haematologist, Aga Khan University Hospital at an event for World Blood Donor Day. This year's theme emphasises the need to improve the safety and sufficiency of blood supplies through 100 per cent voluntary unpaid donations. In countries like Pakistan that have still to reach this target, initiatives such as community blood drives and young people's involvement are needed to help phase out replacement donation, mainly from relatives, and do away with paid donation.",
